{
  "title": "MZM link with NMOS driver",
  "group": "Links & receivers",
  "schematic": {
    "notes": [
      {
        "x": 60,
        "y": -88,
        "title": "MZM link with NMOS driver — what this testbench does",
        "lines": [
          "Pulse source VIN1 (0->3.3 V) drives NMOS MN1 as an",
          "inverting modulator driver. Pull-up RB1 from supply V1",
          "sets MN1's drain (probe vdrv), which swings the MZM MZM1",
          "arm around Vpi = 3.3 V. CD1 is the drain load cap.",
          "MZM1 modulates laser LAS1; light goes down FIB1 to",
          "photodiode PD1, then TIA OA1 + RF1 gives vout.",
          "",
          "Set CD1.C = 5e-13 and re-run to see the vdrv edges slow",
          "and the received eye (vout) close from limited bandwidth."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "instances": {
